From fe3caf6fefaeef8aa0bb093a1b75fa11fac2eb7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:31:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Specialize native score addressing without an output-buffer
 round trip

Upstream-base: d9f9a0076af0dfcd64f675eac006547d73b29483, after candidate-38 and selected-logit source c88a692e98.

Rationale: the controlled v4 run exposes a BF16 large-batch penalty from gathering through output before normalization. Read selected logits once at the final store, and derive addressing from the input's existing compact, row-padded, column-sliced or transposed layout. Keep general strides for other valid views. This changes address expressions only, not storage, and prepares every specialization before cache freeze.

Quality: no dtype/layout materialization, extra allocation or precision change; the score reduction and final arithmetic retain their original order. All views read their original token-id buffer.

Tests: expand native-input numerical and startup-freeze coverage to padded and fully general views. Full GPU correctness, repeated paired timing and IKET qualification remain required; results are recorded by the deployment experiment.

Upstream-status: local candidate, not submitted upstream.
